  pub let thermal_zone_row_ac : (u64, u64) -> u64 !{mem} @{} =
    fn (row_id: u64) (which: u64) -> unsafe {
      effects: {mem}, capabilities: {},
      justification: "R31.M2-001 (#1094): active trip `which` (0..2) of a live row in deci-Kelvin, 0 if that level was not declared, THERMAL_DECODE_BAD for a dead row or which > 2. `which` is a LEVEL INDEX and not a temperature: it selects among three thresholds the row already holds, so a caller supplying it cannot reach a value the row does not contain -- which is why this is the one accessor in the file that takes a second argument at all. Packed _AC0 [15:0] | _AC1 [31:16] | _AC2 [47:32]; the shift is which*16, computed as two shifts (which << 4) since paideia-as has no mul. Labels prefixed tz_ra_ per reserved-label discipline.",
      block: {
